{ "explanation": "## Why the Sine Graph is Wavy

The sine graph looks like a wave because sine measures something that goes around and around: **the height of a point traveling on a circle**.

Imagine a point moving counterclockwise around a unit circle. Its height above the center is exactly `sin(θ)`, where θ is the angle swept so far. As the point travels:

- **0 → π/2**: height grows from 0 up to 1 (the wave rises to its peak)
- **π/2 → π**: height shrinks back to 0 (the wave falls back to the axis)
- **π → 3π/2**: the point dips *below* the center, height goes to −1 (the wave troughs)
- **3π/2 → 2π**: height returns to 0 (the wave completes one cycle)

Then it repeats — forever. Since circular motion is smooth and periodic, the unrolled "height history" is a smooth, repeating curve: **the sine wave**. The wiggles aren't randomness — they're the fingerprint of rotation!

The animation below shows exactly this: drag the angle slider (or hit Play) and watch the point on the circle trace its height onto the graph to the right.", "manimCode": "// ---- Left: unit circle with rotating point. Right: unrolled sine graph ----

const cx = -3.2, cy = 0.4, R = 1.6;          // circle center & radius
let theta = 0;                                // current angle

// Circle
const circle = new Circle({ radius: R, color: BLUE });
circle.moveTo([cx, cy, 0]);

// Horizontal diameter (baseline for height)
const baseline = new Polygon({
  vertices: [[cx - R, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]],
  color: GRAY
});
baseline.setStrokeWidth(2).setFillOpacity(0);

// Radius arm from center to moving point
const arm = new Polygon({
  vertices: [[cx, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]],
  color: YELLOW
});
arm.setStrokeWidth(3).setFillOpacity(0);

// The moving point on the circle
const dot = new Dot({ point: [cx + R, cy, 0], color: YELLOW });

// Dashed "height" line from the point down to the baseline
const heightLine = new Polygon({
  vertices: [[cx + R, cy, 0], [cx + R, cy, 0]],
  color: YELLOW_D
});
heightLine.setStrokeWidth(2).setFillOpacity(0);

// Dashed projection line from the circle point over to the graph
const projLine = new Polygon({
  vertices: [[cx + R, cy, 0], [1.2, cy, 0]],
  color: GRAY
});
projLine.setStrokeWidth(1).setFillOpacity(0);

// ---- Right: the sine graph (one full period) ----
const ax = new Axes({
  xRange: [0, 2 * Math.PI, Math.PI / 2],
  yRange: [-1.5, 1.5, 0.5],
  xLength: 5.4,
  yLength: 3.2,
  tips: false
});
ax.moveTo([3.9, -0.6, 0]);
const xLabels = ax.getAxisLabels();

// Traced-so-far portion of the sine curve (rebuilt as theta changes)
let trace = ax.plot(x => Math.sin(x), {
  color: BLUE,
  xRange: [0, Math.max(theta, 0.001)],
  numSamples: 200
});

// Ghost of the full wave
const fullWave = ax.plot(x => Math.sin(x), { color: BLUE, opacity: 0.15 });

// Dot on the graph at (theta, sin theta)
const graphDot = new Dot({ point: ax.c2p(0, 0), color: YELLOW });

// ---- Labels ----
const title = new Text({ text: "Sine = height on a circle", color: WHITE, fontSize: 30 });
title.moveTo([0, 3.3, 0]);

const sinLabel = new MathTex({ latex: "\\sin(\\theta)" });
await sinLabel.waitForRender();
sinLabel.nextTo(ax, UP);
sinLabel.shift(scaleVec(1.4, RIGHT));
sinLabel.setColor(BLUE);

const angleLabel = new Text({ text: "θ = 0.00 rad", color: YELLOW, fontSize: 22 });
angleLabel.moveTo([cx, cy + R + 0.6, 0]);

// ---- Rebuild everything that depends on theta ----
function refresh() {
  const px = cx + R * Math.cos(theta);
  const py = cy + R * Math.sin(theta);

  dot.moveTo([px, py, 0]);
  arm.setVertices([[cx, cy, 0], [px, py, 0]]);
  heightLine.setVertices([[px, py, 0], [px, cy, 0]]);
  projLine.setVertices([[px, py, 0], [ax.c2p(theta, Math.sin(theta))[0], py, 0]]);

  graphDot.moveTo(ax.c2p(theta, Math.sin(theta)));

  scene.remove(trace);
  trace = ax.plot(x => Math.sin(x), {
    color: BLUE,
    xRange: [0, Math.max(theta, 0.001)],
    numSamples: 200
  });
  scene.add(trace);

  const pos = angleLabel.getCenter();
  scene.remove(angleLabel);
  const fresh = new Text({
    text: "θ = " + theta.toFixed(2) + " rad",
    color: YELLOW,
    fontSize: 22
  });
  fresh.moveTo(pos);
  scene.add(angleLabel = fresh);
}

scene.add(title, circle, baseline, fullWave, trace, ax, xLabels,
          projLine, heightLine, arm, dot, graphDot, sinLabel, angleLabel);

// ---- Controls: slider + play button ----
const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'bottom-left', width: 280 });

controls.addSlider({
  label: 'Angle θ',
  min: 0,
  max: 2 * Math.PI,
  value: 0,
  step: 0.02,
  onChange: (v) => {
    theta = v;
    refresh();
  }
});

let playing = false;
controls.addButton({
  label: '▶ Play rotation',
  onClick: () => { playing = !playing; }
});
controls.addButton({
  label: 'Reset',
  onClick: () => {
    theta = 0;
    playing = false;
    refresh();
  }
});

// ---- Animation loop for the play button ----
let last = performance.now();
function loop(now) {
  if (playing) {
    theta += (now - last) / 1000 * 1.2;   // ~1.2 rad per second
    if (theta >= 2 * Math.PI) {
      theta = 2 * Math.PI;
      playing = false;
    }
    refresh();
  }
  last = now;
  requestAnimationFrame(loop);
}
requestAnimationFrame(loop);

await scene.wait(999999);" }

